# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One Backlog space = one <PREFIX>_SPACE + <PREFIX>_API_KEY pair.
# The space name is the lowercase prefix (ACME_* -> space "acme").
# Put this file at $BACKLOG_BRIDGE_HOME/.env (default ~/.config/backlog-bridge/.env), outside the repo,
# and chmod 600 it.
# _SPACE: for xxx.backlog.com write just "xxx"; for .backlog.jp or other hosts write the full host,
#         e.g. "xxx.backlog.jp".
# Get a key: Personal Settings -> API -> Register new API key (on EACH space).
# Do NOT put a comment on the same line as a value.
# Optional shell variables: BACKLOG_BRIDGE_HOME, BACKLOG_BRIDGE_CONFIG, BACKLOG_BRIDGE_PROFILE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Uncomment and fill in one pair per space.

# Your own (internal) Backlog
# INTERNAL_SPACE=yourcompany
# INTERNAL_API_KEY=

# A customer's Backlog
# ACME_SPACE=acme.backlog.jp
# ACME_API_KEY=

# How YOU review text before it is sent to a customer (personal — keep it in your own .env):
#   bilingual = you read the customer's language: review a bilingual draft, only the customer's language is sent
#   translate = you don't: review in your own language only; the agent translates and sends right away
# Uncomment ONE of them — until it is set, the agent asks you which applies.
# BACKLOG_BRIDGE_REVIEW=bilingual
# BACKLOG_BRIDGE_REVIEW=translate
# Your language and the customers' language (defaults: vi / ja)
# BACKLOG_BRIDGE_LANG=vi
# BACKLOG_BRIDGE_CUSTOMER_LANG=ja
